<http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain/0.2.0> .
<http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Air Domain Ontology"@en .
<http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "An OWL 2 DL ontology of the civil air transport domain: passenger and cargo operations, airports, aircraft and airworthiness, flight operations and crew, air traffic management, ground handling, regulation, safety and security, and environmental sustainability."@en .
<http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Air Domain Ontology"@en .
<http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "air" .
<http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain#" .
<http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A comprehensive ontology of the civil air transport domain, covering air passenger and cargo/freight operations, airport infrastructure and operations, aircraft and airworthiness, flight operations and crew, air traffic management, ground handling, regulatory/certification instruments, safety and security, and environmental sustainability. Consolidated from the project's existing class/relationship tables (Air_Freight_and_Passenger_Ontology, Sheet3 organisational/regulatory layers, the cargo-handling 'Category' breakdown, and the Airport Operations Plan / APOC concepts) and extended with generally-recognised air-domain concepts not yet captured there. No upper ontology (e.g. BFO) is imported; a small set of pragmatic top-level classes (Agent, PhysicalObject, InformationObject, Process, Location, PolicyOrRegulation, Measurement, Service, Category) organises the hierarchy instead."@en .
<http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Air Domain Ontology"@en .
<http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "0.2.0" .
<http://www.cranfield.ac.uk/ontology/air-domain> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> "0.2.0: fixed inverted/part-of subclass links (Aerodrome/Airport, AerodromeOperatingSite, ChargingPoint, Consignment); converted EASA, FAA, ICAO, IATA, CORSIA from classes to individuals; moved classifications out of Measurement into a new Category branch; added Identifier, Certificate, Licence, Occurrence, TradeAssociation, GroundVehicle; fixed IATAcode/ICAOcode range typos and over-narrow domains/ranges; added part-of, property hierarchy, inverses, functional properties, existential and cardinality restrictions, defined classes and disjointness axioms."@en .
